  "answer": "Before promising enterprise deployment dates, sales should verify a pre-sales checklist that includes:\n\n- **Corpus Readiness Checklist:** Share it during discovery and specifically highlight scanned PDF/OCR requirements so the customer understands the 8–10 week Enterprise timeline and any delay risk. [NL-023-S07] [NL-015-S04]\n- **Mandatory pre-onboarding format audit:** Require the prospect to submit ~20 core documents for format analysis; if scanned PDFs are present, flag this early so Customer Success can adjust the target timeline. [NL-031-S06]\n- **Enterprise implementation blockers:** Confirm readiness for Active Directory permission mapping, SSO/security review, and data cleanup/scanned PDF handling, because these are the main drivers of the 8.7-week actual median and rollout delays. [NL-015-S04]\n- **Standard Enterprise timeline expectation:** Use the 8–10 week target with the understanding that success depends on executive alignment and pre-cleared security/SSO. [NL-031-S02]\n- **Roadmap and integration dates:** Consult Sofia Almeida or the official Product Roadmap for upcoming features/integrations, do not guarantee launch dates, and frame roadmap dates as targets, not contractual guarantees. [NL-009-S08] Management is enforcing that sales must not promise immediate Teams support. [NL-016-S05]\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer  \nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
